  "family": "pop",
  "lineage": "Softer-romantic style of salsa developed in mid-1980s Miami and New York from older salsa dura. Reduced rhythmic-aggression, simpler arrangements, slower-mid-tempo, explicit romantic-love-and-relationship lyric content. Emerged through Latin-Caribbean commercial-radio-targeting and became dominant late-1980s-and-1990s salsa-mainstream. RMM Records and producer Sergio George consolidated canonical sound.",
